## Original Content
Canadian political leaders stepped up their rhetoric on Monday in response to the latest US tariff threats.

## Summary
Canadian political leaders intensified their criticism on Monday in response to new US tariff threats, using sharper language to express opposition. The escalation in rhetoric indicates growing frustration with the trade measures. This development highlights tensions between Canada and the US over tariffs.

## Key Points
- Canadian politicians escalated their rhetoric in response to US tariffs.
- The sharpened tone was specifically directed at recent tariff threats from the US.
- The phrase 'Enough is enough' signifies a firm stance against the measures.


